I'll explore the relevant components first.Now I have everything I need. Let me write the redesigned Files mode component.Now let me refine it (lazy-load the heavy diff renderer + fix the nested-interactive header):## Files mode — new vs. changed rendering

**Direct recommendation:** the Files view now decides per block: a file that does not exist on disk (or a `change_type="new"` envelope) renders its **content**; a file that already exists renders the **diff** against the on-disk version. All the decision logic lives in the Files-view component (`MessageFileView.vue`), so `ChatEntry.vue` itself needs no change — it only toggles `showFileView`.

### Specifications

| Area | Decision |
|---|---|
| **Default view** | `new` → content · `modified` → diff · `deleted` → content (red card) |
| **Detection order** | `change_type` from `<file_change>` → `files.read()` (missing/empty = new) → `files.diff()` for stats |
| **Toggle** | Per-card switch (content ⇄ diff) appears only when both sides exist; a manual toggle wins over the default |
| **Status tokens** | New = `badge-success` / `border-success/40` · Changed = `badge-warning` / `border-warning/40` · Deleted = `badge-error` / `border-error/40` |
| **Density** | Card header 1 line, body capped at `max-h-[480px]` with scroll; per-card + expand/collapse all |
| **Stats** | `+insertions` (`text-success`) / `-deletions` (`text-error`) parsed from the diff response, `tabular-nums` |
| **Actions** | Toggle view · Copy · Add to chat · Sub-task · Save (`btn-success btn-outline`) — all `@click.stop` so the header collapse never fires |
| **Motion** | None added beyond DaisyUI defaults; chevron/state changes are instant (no >300 ms micro-animations) |

### Implementation highlights
- **One card per code block**, keyed `${path}#${index}` — the same key `ChatEntry` already uses for bulk selection, so selections, expanded state and the loaded status survive streaming re-renders.
- **DiffViewer is lazy-loaded** (`defineAsyncComponent`): Monaco + `@git-diff-view` never enter the chunk that renders every chat message (same guard `CodeViewer` uses).
- **Streaming guard:** while `message.done === false` nothing is requested (a half-written file must not be diffed); `watch('message.done')` re-resolves the cards when the message finishes.
- **Project scoping:** `project` prop → `message.project_id` → chat project → active project, so reads/writes/saves hit the project the block paths belong to.
- **Bulk-save toolbar untouched:** `selectionKeys` / `selectedKeys` / `toggle-select` are still honoured, checkboxes render only for writable blocks.

### Anti-patterns avoided
- ❌ Diffing a file that does not exist (the old `:diff-option="true"` forced the diff view for **every** block).
- ❌ Nested interactive elements: the row is a plain click target, the chevron is a real focusable `<button>`.
- ❌ Per-block `CodeViewer` chrome (edit / rollback / zoom) inside a review list — Files mode is now a review surface, not an editor.

### Accessibility checklist
- [x] Every icon button has `aria-label` (+ DaisyUI tooltip for sighted users)
- [x] Expand/collapse exposes `aria-expanded`
- [x] Selection checkbox has `aria-label="Select <file>"`
- [x] Status is never colour-only — icon **and** text badge ("New" / "Changed" / "Deleted")
- [x] Skeleton has `aria-hidden="true"` so it is not announced
- [x] Keyboard: all actions reachable; Ctrl+F-free reading (content/diff scroll containers)

